      "math_academy_id": "q-72732",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Suppose $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(B)=102.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-\\frac{1}{2}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 102 \\\\  & =-51.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
